data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":839,"item_id":"msg_017085b9fa06899a016b027aefcebc87d1a4a9eedcd48af115","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"moss\",\"decision\":\"develop\",\"ability\":null,\"reason\":\"The existing resting-shelter interface already provides the requested physical inspection, but its demonstrated reference-unavailable failures do not distinguish reference resolution from material eligibility. The supplied state contains the owned branch item-112-moss-648; this establishes a reference worth resolving, not its structural suitability. Develop a repair and diagnostic extension to the existing interface rather than a duplicate shelter capability. The precise failure cause must be established in implementation.\",\"specification\":\"Patch resting-shelter through the current implementation handoff; record code reuse separately from the diagnostic extension. Preserve its existing physical laws, material requirements, costs and mastery. Public schema remains {mode,project,target,materials,x,y,angle}; inspect accepts a canonical exact item ID or one item: prefix followed by that ID, resolving both to the same persistent identity. Use the authoritative inventory for owned targets, not a ground-only or remembered-object lookup; owned-item access must not depend on stale pickup coordinates. Reachable structures still require actual shared-geometry distance <=0.65. Validate references separately from eligibility: return structured reasonCode, suppliedReference, resolvedId when available, required condition and observed obstruction, distinguishing malformed reference, absent or inaccessible identity, wrong ownership, insufficient quantity, unsuitable material, unavailable geometry and record-capacity obstruction. Report only personally accessible candidates; an empty candidate list must not imply material unsuitability. Missing physical dimensions remain unknown, not fabricated or conflated with lookup failure. Successful inspection takes one performed round and 0.2 energy, consumes no material, and records only observable geometry, condition, source lineage and explicit uncertainties; it does not certify load capacity or authorize construction without the existing paid tests. Preflight resolution failures consume no physical inspection effort; interrupted paid work retains actual expenditure. Declare shelter-reference-diagnostic for reference/eligibility results and retain shelter-inspected for completed physical inspections, with canonical identity, paid effort and observed fields in replay. Persist diagnostic version and operation IDs. Inspection has one remaining work stage, completes exactly once, and has no material escrow. Global pause preserves progress; death or cancellation stops unfinished work without producing a completed observation. Preserve all existing multi-round shelter work, installed components, remaining stages and escrow ownership; cancellation or death releases only surviving uninstalled escrow once, without cloning, deletion or refunds. Migrate existing records and active operations without resetting progress, granting supplies or altering historical failures. Regression-test the supplied owned branch reference in both accepted forms, partial specimens, inaccessible targets, unknown geometry and full project capacity without advancing the live simulation. Never silently archive records or require a new project merely to resolve an existing inspection target. Existing shelter mastery remains valid; the one-round study duration applies only to learning the added diagnostic contract, not to restoring access to previously mastered inspection.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Reference repair, diagnostics, registration and study produce no wellbeing reward: resolving an interface fault is not itself a beneficial physical experience or experimental discovery. A subsequently completed paid inspection may qualify for the existing grounded-understanding source only if it actually establishes new, supported material information for the inspecting actor. Subscribe to information-confirmed from resting-shelter with qualified=true: transient amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8 rounds, refresh cooldown 12 rounds; maintained gain 0.035 per qualifying event with existing decay 0.0015 and the source's bounded saturation. Repeated known observations and diagnostic messages do not qualify. Reuse this source without an alias or additional practice reward. Shelter comfort and personal-refuge feedback remain contingent on actual completed shelter and beneficial occupied rest; this repair supplies neither.\",\"visualReview\":\"Show the resolved canonical item identity and a clear separation between reference status, observable material condition and unresolved suitability. Bind diagnostic panels to shelter-reference-diagnostic and completed inspection records to shelter-inspected; replay must show actual effort and measured observations, not a successful test animation for a failed lookup. Retain existing item geometry and shelter rendering. No new object, structural collision, shade, insulation or refuge appearance is created by this patch.\",\"learning\":1}]}","logprobs":[]}

